<div class="erp-status">
    {if $erp_foreign_found}
        <div class="alert alert-warning">
            {l s='The back office already has another Referrer-Policy header set from PHP and the module leaves it untouched. Its value:' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}
            <strong>{$erp_foreign_value|escape:'html':'UTF-8'}</strong>
        </div>
    {/if}
    {if $erp_too_late}
        <div class="alert alert-warning">
            {l s='The header could not be sent on this page because output had already started: look for a PHP notice or stray characters printed by another module.' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}
        </div>
    {/if}
    {if $erp_multishop}
        <div class="alert alert-info">
            {l s='Multistore: the shop settings are saved for the selected shop context; the back office settings are global.' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}
        </div>
    {/if}
    <div class="alert alert-info">
        {if $erp_front_enabled}
            {l s='Shop: the header is sent with the value' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}
            <strong class="erp-value-front">{$erp_front_policy|escape:'html':'UTF-8'}</strong>
        {else}
            {l s='Shop: the header is switched off.' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}
        {/if}
        <br>
        {if $erp_back_enabled}
            {l s='Back office: the header is sent with the value' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}
            <strong class="erp-value-back">{$erp_back_policy|escape:'html':'UTF-8'}</strong>
        {else}
            {l s='Back office: the header is switched off.' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}
        {/if}
    </div>
    <p class="help-block">{l s='Choose the value for each area in its tab and save.' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}</p>
    <div class="panel erp-help">
        <a href="#" class="erp-help-toggle" data-erp-target="erp-help-body" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="erp-help-body">
            <i class="icon-question-circle"></i>
            {l s='Help / how it works' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}
        </a>
        <div id="erp-help-body" class="erp-help-body">
            <ul>
                <li>{l s='The module adds the Referrer-Policy header to the pages generated by PrestaShop: the shop, the back office and its login page.' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}</li>
                <li>{l s='The header tells the browser how much of the current address it may reveal to the next page and to third-party resources (images, scripts, fonts).' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}</li>
                <li>{l s='If another Referrer-Policy header has already been set from PHP (a future native PrestaShop option or another module), the module neither replaces nor duplicates it.' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}</li>
                <li>{l s='A header added by the web server itself (Apache, nginx, a CDN) cannot be seen from PHP: if your server already sends one, switch this module off for that area or remove it from the server, so that only one is sent.' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}</li>
                <li>{l s='Static files (images, CSS, JavaScript) are served by the web server without going through PrestaShop, so they do not carry the header. This is expected: the policy that counts is the one of the page.' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}</li>
                <li>{l s='With no-referrer the browser also sends the header Origin: null when a form is submitted. PrestaShop does not check it, but if a firewall or another module does, use same-origin in the back office.' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}</li>
                <li>{l s='To check it, open the developer tools of the browser, go to the Network tab, click the request of the page and look for Referrer-Policy among the response headers.' d='Modules.Ecomreferrerpolicy.Admin'}</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
